WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.800
I did more for the black community

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:07.150
than anybody with the possible
exception of Abraham Lincoln.

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.650
All men and women were created by

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:11.360
(stuttering) you know the thing.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.440
Is it any wonder that neither Joe Biden

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.090
nor Donald Trump can crack fifty percent

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:17.370
in approval ratings?

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:19.980
They're cringeinducing to everyone except

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.720
hardcore partisans.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.190
Why the hell would I take
a test? Are you a joke?

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.660
No religion, no anything.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.540
Hurt the Bible, hurt God.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.120
Which is why just 31% of Americans

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:35.840
identify as Democrats and
only 26% as Republicans.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.950
41% say they're politically independent.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:41.190
The major parties are selling Americans

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:44.430
on policy bundles that are utterly inane.

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:47.920
If you want tax cuts, you
have to vote against abortion,

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:50.520
in favor of billions more
in military spending,

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.250
and against immigration.

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:54.640
If you want to vote in
favor of immigration,

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:58.020
you have to also sign on to
a $2 trillion Green New Deal,

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:00.650
trapping children in
failing school districts,

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:02.350
and massive tax hikes.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:04.850
It's no surprise that
typical American voters

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:07.140
are looking more and more
like Bridget Phetasy,

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:09.430
a podcaster and comedian who has written

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:11.760
the battle cry of the politically homeless

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.740
and explained in a recent column

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.760
why she won't be voting at all this fall.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.250
Her reasons? If Trump
wins, America will burn.

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:22.119
And if Trump loses, America will burn.

00:01:22.119 --> 00:01:23.940
The thing that drives me crazy is just

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:26.150
the blatant lying, it's the same thing.

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:28.630
And I'm at the point
where I'm not even sure.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:30.840
Does he know he's lying?

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:33.120
I couldn't even listen to him speak.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:36.400
With Biden, I feel terror.
You know, I feel like

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:39.270
Oh God, when's he going to
lose his train of thought?

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:41.720
And I feel like I can see
that terror in his eyes

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:45.080
when all of sudden he hits
kind of a blank patch.

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:47.020
Phetasy is typical of Americans

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:49.830
in that she's socially
liberal on many issues.

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:52.410
I do believe it's empowering

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:55.820
to be able to sleep
with whomever you want.

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:57.440
And conservative on others.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:59.000
I just like, laugh at the fact

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:04.000
that we're having conversations
about, serious debates about

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:05.820
whether girls and boys are different.

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:08.180
And aware more generally of the limits

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:09.350
of her own expertise.

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:11.220
Then I just stopped and realized

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:13.700
I knew absolutely nothing about guns.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.830
I didn't how to load a gun, hold a gun.

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:19.847
I didn't know any of our
gun laws in California.

00:02:19.847 --> 00:02:23.410
I knew nothing. And I was
just spouting my mouth off

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:24.730
as if I did.

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:26.220
She's neither Republican red

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:29.540
nor Democrat blue, but an alienated mix.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:31.890
Oh yeah, I'm totally a purple person.

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:36.860
I really try to take everything
on a casebycase basis.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:38.790
She also hates how politics has become

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:42.660
all about shutting down dialogue
and dwelling on resentment.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:47.660
What I've seen on the left
is just a complete inability

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.700
to sooth the cognitive
dissonance that happened

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:53.690
when Trump won the election.

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:57.410
And instead of accepting
what is and moving forward,

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:01.320
and saying, how can we
rebuild, what did we do wrong?

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:05.130
They doubled down, called
even more people racist,

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:08.160
lost more allies, alienated more people

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:09.900
who should be allies in this,

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:12.880
and closed the tent even more.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.350
There's identity politics
on the right as well,

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:18.188
and there's a lot of grievance that I see.

00:03:18.188 --> 00:03:19.970
Unless Democrats and Republicans

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.150
start speaking to people like Phetasy,

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:23.810
their ranks will keep shrinking

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:26.200
and they'll have to eke
out narrow victories

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:29.480
based on scaring voters
with insane claims.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:30.920
If you have a problem figuring out

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:33.120
whether you're for me or Trump,

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.020
then you ain't black.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:35.840
If I don't win the election,

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.570
China will own the United States.

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:41.100
You're going to have to
learn to speak Chinese.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.840
Politics needs the same
diversity of offerings

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:45.806
that the internet has
brought to the media.

00:03:45.806 --> 00:03:47.376
Bridget!

00:03:47.376 --> 00:03:48.209
[Bridget Phetasy] Heyo.

00:03:48.209 --> 00:03:49.303
[Interviewer] You're here. You made it.

00:03:49.303 --> 00:03:51.390
I came to make a citizen's arrest.

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:53.420
What I'm hearing from people basically

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.620
is that they're done with
the mainstream media.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:58.650
So I don't know how much
longer the mainstream media has

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:01.330
because they behave like
New Media doesn't exist.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:03.500
They act like the internet doesn't exist.

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:06.480
I see all of these things,
even just my inbox,

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:09.090
with all of these thoughtful messages

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:12.070
of why they migrated politically

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:15.850
and what that story is,
whether it's from red to blue

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:17.770
or blue to red, or independent.

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:21.200
I would say I see a lot of potential

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.720
and I see a lot of reasons to be hopeful.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:28.580
And there's so much conversation
happening in the middle.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:33.510
I do believe that although
we might have to choose

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:36.150
or people feel they have
to choose in this binary,

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:39.380
that the center is not only holding

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:41.880
but kind of coalescing in weird ways

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:45.443
that might not really be apparent
until after this election.

